  "solution": {
    "text": "When pulley has a finite mass <math><mi>M</mi></math> and radius <math><mi>R</mi></math>, then tension in two segments of the string are different.<br /><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/ci/image25-8e2c543b-b2b7-4dbb-a4bb-ec438590c74b.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 138px; height: 190px;\" /><br /><br />Here, <math><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>T</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfrac><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>g</mi></math>",
